Overlay patch 0025 (rev2): synchronous resource-load probe with per-window
AGGREGATES and failure-path timing. Round 1 falsified the single-big-file
hypothesis (4 windows with 100-560 ms frames, zero >10 ms loads during
them) and exposed two probe holes: bursts of small loads sum invisibly
under a per-file threshold, and failed alt-pack lookups early-return
before the timer (a texture pack makes EVERY load try alt/ first). rev2
accumulates all load time + count into atomics the 0008 probe reports as
load_ms/loads per window; >10 ms singles still log named (MISS-tagged for
failures). Cache hits still pay nothing. __IOS__-only.

--- a/libultraship/src/ship/resource/ResourceManager.cpp
+++ b/libultraship/src/ship/resource/ResourceManager.cpp
@@ -1,5 +1,20 @@
 #include "ship/resource/ResourceManager.h"
 #include <spdlog/spdlog.h>
+#ifdef __IOS__
+#include <atomic>
+#include <chrono>
+// SOH_IOS (overlay 0025 rev2): per-window aggregate of synchronous load
+// time — round 1 proved single loads rarely cross 10 ms, but a burst of
+// small loads (room transition) or failed alt-pack lookups can sum to a
+// 100-600 ms frame invisibly. The 0008 probe reads/resets via
+// SohIos_LoadStats.
+static std::atomic<uint64_t> sSohIosLoadUs{ 0 };
+static std::atomic<uint32_t> sSohIosLoadCount{ 0 };
+extern "C" void SohIos_LoadStats(float* ms, unsigned int* count) {
+    *ms = (float)(sSohIosLoadUs.exchange(0) / 1000.0);
+    *count = sSohIosLoadCount.exchange(0);
+}
+#endif
 #include "ship/resource/File.h"
 #include "ship/resource/archive/Archive.h"
 #include <algorithm>
